  message: "Batch 5a: on okhttp and detekt-core the class_hint mark went from 530 to 2,318 resolved Kotlin calls once the Kotlin analyzer reports constructions and calls instead of binding by name (2,033 of them on calls nothing resolved before). A blind judge read 15 of the new ones: 14 right, 1 the right type with the wrong overload. The Kotlin worker read 10: 9 right, 1 wrong (chunkSizes.add(..), a library name: this linker does not read stdlib_member_name; not changed in the batch because one measured edge did not justify moving the pilot languages). The linker now skips a stub an earlier linker resolved (30 wrong second edges on jedis and commons-compress before that). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/batch5a_11262026/judge/."  # 59b4
